Overview 
Problem: 
Product tutorial videos quickly become outdated as UI changes are released. Current tutorial maintenance requires manual rerecording, editing, narration updates, and post-production work, which is resource intensive and difficult to scale for fast moving product teams. 

Goal: preserve existing high-quality edited tutorials while minimizing manual re-editing effort.  

Process flow 
Input: old tutorial, new screen recording 
Step 1: Segment tutorial, edited regions 
Step 2: Detect UI Element targets in original video
Step 3: Locate equivalent elements in new UI
Step 5: For those elements add editing of zoom, highlighting, cropping, timing
Step 6: merge back with original video tutorial
Step 7: export draft tutorial as video, make changes in the Akool video production for further editing 

Design of Segmentation Detection: 
UI semantic diffing - categorize differences of UI regions 
OpenCV  - detect visual differences
LLM model analysis - describe visual differences 
DOM-awarness 

Step 1: Segment tutorial and detect edited regions 
Dedect cuts / transitions 
Identify tutorial workflow sections / features of the tool 
Identify edited regions 
Zooms 
Crops
Highlights
Motion emphasis 
Cursor focus 
Output: 
Timeline segmented map 
Edit metadata
Step 2: Detect UI element targets in original video 
Identify important elements refereced by 
Cursor 
Narration 
Zoom target
Highlight overlaws 
Output: semantic UI target map 

Step 3: location equivalent or new elements in updated UI / new video 
Compare original UI states against new UI states 
Identify equivalent interface elements 
Map old workflow -> new workflow 
Tools 
Multimodal LLM analysis 
Visual similarity matching 
DOM-aware mapping(?) 
Step 4: Semantic UI diffing 
Compare UI changes by category 
What kind of change was made to an element 
What is the new feature? 
Ex. layout change, renaming element 

Step 5: Reconstruct editing 
Preserve aspects of original tutorial video behavior
Transfer editing, re-anchor edits to updated UI positions, preserve pacing and visual consistency 

Step 6: Merge Updated Segments into original tutorial 
Replace outdated clips only 
Clone voice for voice feature explanations 
Output: updated draft tutorial timeline 

Step 7: export into akool video production pipeline 
Output to include editable timeline/ project data 


Core technical compontnes 

Video segmentation engine 
Purpose to break tutorial into meaningful workflow sections 
Tools: openCV, 
Responsibilities: 
Cut detection, scene segmentation, workflow chunking, narration alignment 
Semantic UI diff engine 
Compare old/new interface states 
Determine if tutorial instructions are invalidated, classify UI changes 
Tools: Open CV visual differentiation, OCR text extraction, multimodal LLM analysis 
Editing Intent Transfer Engine 
Detect cropped regions, highlights, zoom targets, timing emphasis 
Reconstruction updated placements 
Narration synchronization 
Transcribe original narration 
Identify outdated instructions 
Regenerate modified narration
Synthesized update audio 



